          <!-- Category intro -->
          <div class="max-w-3xl mb-6">
            <h2 class="text-[clamp(24px,2.5vw,44px)] font-bold text-gray-900 mb-3 font-barlow-condensed">Active Harmonic Filter (AHF) Series</h2>
            <p class="text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-gray-600 mb-2">Every CHITEK AHF compensates harmonics from the 2nd through the 50th order, and you decide how much of each individual order gets corrected. The compensation current tracks whatever the network is producing at that moment instead of running to a fixed curve — cleaner power, less wasted energy.</p>
            <p class="text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-gray-600">No two loads distort the waveform the same way, and a single load keeps changing its harmonic signature as operating conditions shift. The filter reads those changes continuously and adapts its output to follow them.</p>
